# Recursive (`**/`) patterns — an unanchored pattern like `dist/` only matches at the repo root in
# Docker's .dockerignore matching, not at every depth (unlike a real .gitignore). Confirmed
# empirically (012 T050 review): a stale nested apps/runner/dist/ (including a leftover
# runner-release.json from a previous local build) and nested node_modules/ were both entering the
# build context via `COPY . .` and getting baked into the image, making every `runner-build` rerun
# non-deterministic relative to the last one — exactly what ADR 0014's "same digest is a legitimate
# no-op" depends on not happening.
**/node_modules
.git/
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.tsbuildinfo
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
